INT. STARSHIP ARGENT DAWN - ENGINE CORE - SHIP NIGHT

A cathedral of glowing pipes and throbbing coils. A yellow warning lamp spins.

COMMANDER HALLORAN, 50s, in a gold-trimmed uniform, grips a rail. DR. XIMENA ROJAS-VANCE, 40s, a physicist with wild gray hair, taps a console. BOSUN TUCK, 60s, a grizzled engineer in oil-stained overalls, hauls on a valve wheel.

HALLORAN
Doctor, how long?

XIMENA
Eleven minutes before the core goes critical.

TUCK
Eleven? I said nine.

XIMENA
Your instruments are older than my daughter, Tuck.

TUCK
They've never lied to me.

ENSIGN RAVI, 20s, in a crisp blue jumpsuit, bursts through the hatch, breathless.

RAVI
Commander! The aft shields are failing!

HALLORAN
Ensign, take the other console.

RAVI
Sir, I haven't been trained --

HALLORAN
Neither was I, when I started.

Ravi darts to the console. Ximena and Tuck both reach for the same lever. Their hands collide. They glare at each other and then, as one, push.

The lamp flares white. The pipes shudder. Halloran braces, Ravi ducks, Tuck is thrown against the wall.

XIMENA
It's working!

TUCK
Don't say that. Saying it jinxes it.

HALLORAN
(quiet)
Bosun. Doctor. Ensign. If we get through this, I'm buying the first round.

RAVI
Sir, is that a promise?

HALLORAN
It's an order.

The core's hum drops to a purr. The warning lamp dims. All four slump, grinning.
